@page
@model MossHarper.Pages.ServicesModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Expertise";
}
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow light">Where we can help</p><h1>Advice grounded in operational experience.</h1><p>Independent, practical support for property and estate challenges.</p></div></section>
<div class="service-detail-list">
<section id="managing-agent" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 01 / Property performance</p><h2>Independent Managing Agent &amp; Operational Reviews</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Independent scrutiny of management performance, service delivery and accountability.</p><p>An effective review looks beyond individual complaints to establish whether the management structure, resources, contracts and reporting arrangements are fit for purpose. Moss Harper can evaluate existing arrangements, identify underlying causes of underperformance and recommend practical changes.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Managing agent performance and service-delivery reviews</li><li>On-site and central staffing structures, responsibilities and reporting</li><li>Contract management, procurement, service standards and value for money</li><li>Operational improvement plans and support with management transitions</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section id="service-charge" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 02 / Financial performance</p><h2>Service Charge Reviews &amp; Financial Performance</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Establishing whether expenditure is appropriate, justified and reflected in the services delivered.</p><blockquote>The objective is not simply to reduce expenditure, but to establish whether costs are appropriate, justified and delivering the intended services.</blockquote><p>Complex service-charge budgets can be difficult to interrogate. We help clients review budgets, cost allocation, procurement arrangements and financial controls, with particular attention to the relationship between expenditure and actual service delivery.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Budget scrutiny, cost allocation and expenditure reviews</li><li>Review of contracts, procurement, staffing and utility costs</li><li>Value-for-money and service-delivery assessments</li><li>Clear, evidence-based recommendations for improvement</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section id="transformation" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 03 / Transformation</p><h2>Strategic &amp; Operational Transformation</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Restructuring teams, improving operating models and strengthening performance through practical change.</p><p>Operational transformation must work in practice, not simply on paper. Drawing on experience of restructuring central and site-based teams, establishing technical functions and introducing digital platforms, we support businesses seeking clearer accountability and more resilient service delivery. This can include interim senior leadership advice, development handover and estate mobilisation, and operational due diligence for acquisitions.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Operating-model reviews and organisational restructuring</li><li>Site-based and central team design, management reporting and accountability</li><li>Technology and process improvement, including resident-facing platforms</li><li>Interim or part-time executive support, management transitions and change oversight</li><li>Developer handover, estate mobilisation and operational due diligence for investors</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section id="building-safety" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 04 / Building safety</p><h2>Building Safety &amp; Regulatory Compliance</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Operational support for higher-risk buildings, building-safety governance and regulator engagement.</p><p>Building safety requires clear responsibility, reliable information and effective coordination across management and specialist disciplines. We assist with the operational and governance challenges of the regime and help clients engage appropriately qualified professionals when technical judgements or statutory certifications are required.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Accountable-person arrangements and building-safety management reviews</li><li>Building Safety Regulator engagement and Building Assessment Certificate process support</li><li>Safety Case Report coordination, resident-engagement arrangements and information governance</li><li>External-wall remediation programme coordination and operational risk review</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section id="heat-networks" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 05 / Energy</p><h2>Heat Networks &amp; Utility Management</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Clarifying performance, costs and responsibilities as heat networks enter Ofgem regulation.</p><p>Heat networks sit where engineering, operating contracts, billing and resident experience meet. Ofgem became the sector regulator in January 2026, and relevant existing heat networks must be registered by 26 January 2027. Moss Harper helps owners, managing agents and RMCs review operational and commercial arrangements, clarify responsibilities and assess readiness, coordinating specialist technical or regulatory input where required.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Operational readiness reviews covering Ofgem registration and consumer-protection requirements</li><li>Operator and maintenance arrangements, contracts and responsibilities</li><li>Heat-network expenditure, billing structures and service-charge implications</li><li>Performance concerns and efficiency reviews with appropriate technical specialists</li><li>Resident communication and practical improvement plans</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section id="resident-engagement" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 06 / Residents</p><h2>Resident Engagement &amp; Communication</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Helping property businesses communicate clearly, respond consistently and rebuild confidence.</p><p>When residents do not know what is happening, why decisions have been made or when matters will be resolved, uncertainty can quickly undermine trust. Effective engagement means providing timely, accurate information, listening to concerns and making responsibilities and progress visible. It is not about defending every decision; it is about demonstrating accountability.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Resident communication and stakeholder-engagement reviews</li><li>Meeting preparation, consultation and communication around major works or building safety</li><li>Complaint-handling, escalation and recurring-issue analysis</li><li>Digital platforms for recording, tracking and communicating progress</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section id="dispute-resolution" class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Service 07 / Early resolution</p><h2>Early Dispute Assessment, Resolution &amp; Tribunal Support</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">Assessing the facts and the respective positions early, before disputes escalate unnecessarily.</p><p>Moss Harper can assess the underlying management, financial and contractual issues, help clients understand the strengths and weaknesses of their position and explore early resolution. Our role is defined before an instruction begins: in a given matter we may provide a neutral assessment or act for one party, including with case preparation or permitted representation before the First-tier Tribunal (Property Chamber), but we will not act as both a neutral expert and an advocate in the same matter.</p><h3>Illustrative areas of support</h3><ul><li>Independent issue assessments for freeholders, managing agents and leaseholders</li><li>Service-charge disputes, factual investigation and early resolution discussions</li><li>Document review, evidence collation and case preparation</li><li>First-tier Tribunal support and permitted representation, with legal specialists involved where needed</li></ul></div></div></section>
</div>
<section class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Protecting what matters</p><h2>Small problems can become reputational ones quickly.</h2></div><div><p>Weak management, unresolved resident concerns and poor communication can expose property businesses to more than additional costs. They can undermine confidence and cause lasting reputational harm.</p><p>In an environment where concerns can spread rapidly through resident networks and social media, our focus is early assessment, constructive intervention and meaningful corrective action.</p><p class="detail-lead">A credible response is more valuable than a defensive one.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="approach section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow light">Why Moss Harper?</p><h2>Identifying the problem is only the beginning.</h2></div><div><p class="detail-lead">The real value lies in knowing how to resolve it.</p><p>Complex property challenges rarely sit within a single professional discipline. They can involve operational failings, financial exposure, technical concerns, stakeholder relationships and reputational risk.</p><p>Clients work directly with senior-level experience, candid judgement and a willingness to challenge assumptions, even when the conclusions are uncomfortable.</p><p>Drawing on established professional relationships, Moss Harper helps clients identify and engage appropriately qualified specialists, bringing together the experience and resources needed to deliver workable solutions.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="service-detail section-pad"><div class="container detail-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our independence</p><h2>Advice without hidden incentives.</h2></div><div><p>We do not accept referral fees, commissions or financial incentives from specialists we recommend. Recommendations are based on suitability, competence and the needs of the assignment.</p><p>We assess potential conflicts before accepting instructions and disclose relevant interests. Where we act for one party, our role is clear from the outset; that is distinct from acting as a neutral expert.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="closing"><div class="container closing-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow light">Start a conversation</p><h2>What challenge are you trying to resolve?</h2></div><a class="button button-cream" asp-page="/Contact" asp-fragment="contact">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
